  {
    "event": {
      "address": "11 Gillett Square, Dalston, London N16 8AZ",
      "all_day": false,
      "category": "music",
      "dedupe_key": "calum-gourlay-big-band-celebrating-burns-night|2027-01-25|vortex-jazz-club",
      "description": "Timings: *Please note each ticket will give you access to the time slot you book for. Please arrive for the door time. 1st Show Doors 7:00 PM, Music 7:30 PM – 1 set of music 2nd Show Doors 9:15 PM, Music 9:45 PM – 1 set of music About: Join Calum Gourlay’s big band for an unforgettable Burn’s Night celebration. Featuring a band comprised of London’s thriving Scottish jazz community, tonight’s gig includes Calum’s own musical arrangements and compositions, comprising striking new material, haunting and evocative melodies as well as reimagined jazz standards. Tickets are limited and include a nip of whiskey to toast Burns’ Immortal memory, the vibrant artistic community in London and our good health. “Here's a bottle and an honest friend! What wad ye wish for mair, man? Wha kens, before his life may end, What his share may be o' care, man. Then catch the moments as they fly, And use them as ye ought, man; Believe me, happiness is shy And comes not ay when sought, man.” A Bottle and Friend - Robert Burns [embed]https://youtu.be/6dYf-QTpvXc?si=ml4UTQ_F9RPHEOCx[/embed]",
